  "result": "All five tests pass.\n\n```\n5 passed in 0.40s\n```\n\n**What I did:** added `kvstore/store.py` implementing the `Store` class from SPEC.md. Nothing under `tests/` was touched, and no commit was made since you didn't ask for one.\n\n**Approach chosen:** B, SQLite. It gives transactional, crash-safe writes and indexed lookups without loading the whole store into memory, which fits a CLI tool that may grow large. I kept the default rollback journal mode rather than WAL, because WAL leaves `-wal` and `-shm` side files and would break the single-file requirement, while the rollback journal is deleted after each commit. Keys are sorted in Python rather than by SQLite's byte-wise collation so ordering matches Python string comparison for arbitrary Unicode.",
